====================================================================
PolyKernel T37 Wave 7: SUMMA matmul mapping + lowering + golden
  Maps polykernel.matmul (and fused-matmul) onto the SUMMA schedule
  on the Todo 35 Grid: a P x P grid, output-stationary C (each PE
  accumulates its C tile in local SRAM), step s broadcasts the A
  panel EAST along every row and the B panel SOUTH along every
  column, each PE accumulates C_tile += A_panel * B_panel via the CE
  FMAC (Todo 35 Pe::Compute().Fma, @fmacs-style outer product). 2
  colors/axis (A0/A1, B0/B1) ping-pong double-buffer. The compute
  rendezvous fires the panel accumulate only after BOTH panels
  arrive: x_done (A complete) -> @activate(compute), y_done (B
  complete) -> @unblock(compute); the compute task is a data task
  bound to TWO rendezvous colors that fires only after BOTH tokens
  arrive (Todo 36 Scheduler). The simulator FUNCTIONALLY EXECUTES the
  tile program (wavelets routed A-east/B-south via dataflow
  receive-and-retransmit), so C is validated vs the fp32 golden under
  contract C (cosine>=0.999, max_rel_err<=1e-2, pcc>=0.99).
  NOTE: a GPU-free functional/cycle SIMULATOR - does NOT compile real
  CSL and does NOT run on Cerebras hardware. CE+FMAC (no FMU/PMU);
  @set_color_config rx/tx; @activate/@block/@unblock (no @compute/
  @data decorators).
  Golden test size: 32x32x32 matmul on a 4x4 grid (8x8 output tiles,
  8-wide K-slab, 4 SUMMA steps); +/-1 inputs (exact in fp16) so the
  FMAC accumulate is bit-exact vs the fp32 reference.
Evidence: ctest -R 'summa|dataflow_correctness' (routing A-east/
          B-south; 2-input rendezvous; ping-pong colors; simulator-
          executed matmul matches golden; broken rendezvous fails).
